\par }{\b\f1\fs20 Instructions for use: 
\par }{\f1\fs20 
\par If you are going to use a hard disk, you need to prepare it: You need to format it in APA and a partition with file system PFS (you can use the DMS utility to create it). This utility detects the HDD a
utomatically and has capacity to format, but not to create partitions at the moment.
\par (When u have HDAdvance installed already.. u dont have to do anything...)
\par 
\par If you press SELECT u will see a menu that explaines the keys. Press SELECT again to leave this screen. 
\par 
\par To change from panels just press LEFT/RIGHT or L2/R2 
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 Erasing files:}{\f1\fs20  Move to the file u want to erase, press X  to select the file, (or SQUARE if you want to take all the files of the directory) and then go to the right panel, and choose DELETE. 
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 Erasing directories:}{\f1\fs20  Move to the folder u want to erase, do not press X (or else u will enter the folder ofcourse)go to the right panel and choose DELETE. (The folder must be empty first i noticed ??? :S )
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 Copy files:}{\f1\fs20  You need to create a directo
ry on your HDD (unless you use root directory). Select the files on the cd/dvd u want to copy to your HDD with square like u did with deleting..then go to 'TO HDD' and go into the folder u made...choose 'COPY' and there u go, all the files u selected from
 your cd/dvd, will now be copied into the folder u made on your HDD.
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 Renaming files or directories:}{\f1\fs20  Position in the directory or file and use RELABEL 
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 REC CDDA:}{\f1\fs20  You need to introduce an Audio CD before u select the tracks to record. It changes to the 
HDD directory where you want to record those tracks and uses option REC CDDA <---- I have no clue what this is about, it didnt get it to work yet :S )
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 SEL ZERO:}{\f1\fs20  Unselect all the files u have selected (duh). (Square = 'select all' )
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 PLAY:}{\f1\fs20  When u selected a file with X, u can hear/play it by choosing PLAY in the right panel. 
\par 
\par - }{\b\f1\fs20 While a song plays:}{\f1\fs20  Use SELECT to change from visualization to the normal player mode.
\par 
\par The controls are: 
\par 
\par L2-> Fast Rewind : Presses briefly to go back a song or keep pressed to rewind within a song. 
\par R2-> Fast Forward: Presses briefly to advance a song or keep pressed to advance within a song. 
\par START-> Pause/Play a song. 
\par LEFT/RIGHT- Lowers or raises the volume. 
\par SELECT: Changes display (list/visual) 
\par TRIANGLE-> Exit 
\par 
\par Note on browser: when u select the HDD, it shows a first list to us of usable partitions (reason by which it takes awhile in showing  this list the first time). It is not possible to use files from different partitions and we must enter a partition (
with X) before being able to use the commandos of management of files
\par }}